arsenic and arctic ice rose 15 times after Montana mining sent metals across continents. This is Planetarian Daily Episode 240. Excavation at an ancient mound, a dip in fossil carbon dioxide, and Alzheimer's mutations that act outside the brain come next. Ice cores from Canada, Greenland, and Russia, according to science news, hold particles that fell as early as 210 BCE, and the work appears in nature sustainability. Layers dated from 1870 to 1940.

