00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.480
Researchers identified the Anaconda Copper Mining Company in southwestern Montana as the

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.060
likely emitter, a smelter that processed copper ore containing arsenic and lead.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.800
Models built from the ice core concentrations tied the spike to that operation.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.360
Devices installed in 1919 cut arsenic emissions by about 60%.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:02.065
Most people assume industrial pollution stays local or regional, yet ice core chemistry

00:01:02.065 --> 00:01:06.445
shows that fine particles travel thousands of kilometers within days or weeks.

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:12.965
Air above any northern latitude carries microscopic traces of past industrial activity that settled

00:01:12.965 --> 00:01:14.945
into snow and became locked in ice.

00:01:15.645 --> 00:01:21.465
Peak output reached an estimated 30 tons of arsenic a day, comparable to one quarter of Chile's

00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:24.225
current national total from more than 20 operations.

00:01:24.225 --> 00:01:24.425
regions.

00:01:24.785 --> 00:01:29.305
Those particles followed prevailing west to east circulation, which is why Russian

00:01:29.305 --> 00:01:31.425
Arctic cores showed smaller increases.

00:01:32.105 --> 00:01:36.505
What remains uncertain is exactly how much of the deposited material later entered food

00:01:36.505 --> 00:01:38.925
webs or drinking water in distant communities.

00:01:40.025 --> 00:01:46.145
Resiloglu Mound in Turkey, in work covered by Fizz.org, was reconstructed before and after

00:01:46.145 --> 00:01:52.625
excavations that ran from 2003 to 2019, with the results published in Geoderma Regional.

00:01:52.625 --> 00:02:00.865
The team combined 1990 aerial photos, 2019 drone surveys, soil data and 24 years of weather records.

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:06.865
They ran the QGO WEPP model on eight hill slopes. On one cemetery slope,

00:02:07.245 --> 00:02:12.885
modeled annual runoff rows from 12.6 to 20.1 millimeters per year after excavation.

00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:18.765
Average annual soil loss increased from 1.1 to 2.1 kilograms per square meter.

00:02:18.765 --> 00:02:23.545
Here, sediment yield rose from about 11 to 21 tons per hectare per year.

00:02:24.456 --> 00:02:29.656
Fossil carbon dioxide from fuel use declined in the Global Carbon Project tally, which

00:02:29.656 --> 00:02:32.076
appears in Earth System Science data discussions.

00:02:32.776 --> 00:02:39.636
The project estimates 42.2 billion tons of carbon dioxide from fossil fuels in 2026, a drop

00:02:39.636 --> 00:02:41.276
of 0.4 percent.

00:02:41.716 --> 00:02:47.396
Oil emissions dropped nearly 2 percent, and natural gas emissions fell 0.3 percent, while

00:02:47.396 --> 00:02:49.936
coal emissions rose 0.6%.

00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:54.956
The decline coincides with the closure of the Strait of Hormuz after the Iran conflict.

00:02:55.556 --> 00:03:01.336
China, the United States, Europe, and Japan each showed roughly 1% drops, and India's

00:03:01.336 --> 00:03:03.756
emissions rose 4.4%.

00:03:03.756 --> 00:03:09.696
Land use changes such as deforestation increased overall carbon dioxide emissions by 1%, despite

00:03:09.696 --> 00:03:10.976
the fossil fuel decline.

00:03:12.055 --> 00:03:16.815
Inherited Alzheimer's mutations disrupted nerve muscle connections in miniature human cell

00:03:16.815 --> 00:03:19.735
systems, in findings covered by science daily.

00:03:20.495 --> 00:03:24.315
Scientists built those systems from human cells that carried the inherited mutations.

00:03:25.035 --> 00:03:29.415
The mutations altered connections between nerves and muscle cells without any brain or

00:03:29.415 --> 00:03:30.635
spinal cord involvement.

00:03:31.255 --> 00:03:34.155
The work used induced pluripotent stem cell models.

00:03:34.695 --> 00:03:39.595
The changes may explain why some patients show balance, walking, and coordination shifts

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.475
years before memory problems appear.

